      ],
      "application_cycle": "annual NOFA",
      "next_deadline": "Cycle: workshops on rating criteria (June, September and October 2026), applications due in winter, Urban County Standing Committee scoring in March (March 20, 2026 for FY 2026-27), public hearing and Board adoption of the Annual Action Plan in May (May 12, 2026), CAPER hearing in September. The FY 2027-28 round opens after the October 29, 2026 criteria workshop.",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "true",
      "layering_notes": "Monterey County's Housing and Community Development Department (HCD, Craig Spencer, Director; Darby Marshall, Housing Program Manager) runs the Inclusionary Housing Ordinance, the Monterey County Housing Trust Fund, PLHA, the Urban County CDBG and HOME programs and County land dispositions; the County Administrative Office Homelessness Strategies and Initiatives Division (CAO-HSI) runs HHAP and the SHARE Center; the Health Department Behavioral Health Bureau holds BHSA; the Coalition of Homeless Services Providers leads the CoC (CA-506, shared with San Benito); and the Housing Authority of the County of Monterey (HACM) and its Development Corporation supply vouchers and develop housing. Salinas, Monterey, Seaside and other entitlement cities run their own programs (Pass 3). countyofmonterey.gov blocks automated access (pages and documents), so records were built from the Legistar web API client 'monterey' and its Granicus attachments, hamonterey.org, chsp.org, zoneomics and HCD tables. HOME is new and small (about $400,000 a year, unincorporated only) and the County has not yet put it into a construction project; it is best viewed as a $400,000 to $1 million soft loan for a tax credit project in a community such as Castroville, Pajaro, Boronda or Chualar. Source is the April 30, 2026 Action Plan public hearing item (Legistar file RES 26-068) with funding recommendations attached; allocation figures from the March 20, 2026 Standing Committee item and the FY 2025-26 CAPER.",
      "source_url": "https://monterey.legistar.com/LegislationDetail.aspx?ID=65394&GUID=3D85FA19-7C13-4550-B10D-B65A387337DD",
